# Reuse Shared Widgets — No Duplicate UI

Before building a custom TextField, Button, Checkbox, Dropdown, Dialog, Image, Error view, or similar:

1. Check `lib/app/widgets/` and existing feature widgets.
2. Prefer the shared widget if it covers the need (compose via params, not a copy).
3. Only create a new widget when no existing one fits — and put it in the right layer (`app/widgets` if reusable app-wide).

## Prefer these

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Text input | `AppTextField` |
| Primary / action button | `AppButton` |
| Icon button | `AppIconButton` |
| Checkbox / radio | `AppCheckbox` / `AppRadioWidget` |
| Dropdown | `AppDropdown` / `DropdownSearchField` |
| Dialog | `AppDialog` / `DialogHelper` |
| Network image | `AppNetworkImage` |
| Pull-to-refresh | `AppRefreshWidget` |

## Do not

- Copy-paste the same layout or form field into multiple screens.
- Use raw `TextField` / `ElevatedButton` / `Checkbox` when an `App*` widget exists and fits.
- Invent a parallel “custom” button/input for one screen when `AppButton` / `AppTextField` work.

Extract shared pieces into one widget and reuse it.
